<http://data.silknow.org/object/b9c49167-e4b1-31c9-82cd-7c7943dda06b>
        a                   ecrm:E73_Information_Object ;
        rdfs:comment        "\"I mestieri delli mode a Venezia\", Venezia, 1997. pàg.100, núm.99: imatge a color. \"Voided velvet. Venice? 14th-15th centuries. On a crimsom ground, Venetian coins (zechini) are made with weft threads of gold wrapped around a yellow silk core; identical fabrics are in Florence and the Orient. The dress of Salome, depicted in a four-teenth-century mosaic in Saint Mark basilica, is made with a textile of this type. Venice, Mesei Civici, Centro Studi di Storia del Tessuto e del Costume, formerly Collection Guggenheim, nr.439\"."@ca ;
        ecrm:P129_is_about  <http://data.silknow.org/object/a44f8894-fdaf-3041-aa30-f0d5f165a89a> ;
        ecrm:P2_has_type    <http://data.silknow.org/information/bibliography> ;
        ecrm:P3_has_note    "\"I mestieri delli mode a Venezia\", Venezia, 1997. pàg.100, núm.99: imatge a color. \"Voided velvet. Venice? 14th-15th centuries. On a crimsom ground, Venetian coins (zechini) are made with weft threads of gold wrapped around a yellow silk core; identical fabrics are in Florence and the Orient. The dress of Salome, depicted in a four-teenth-century mosaic in Saint Mark basilica, is made with a textile of this type. Venice, Mesei Civici, Centro Studi di Storia del Tessuto e del Costume, formerly Collection Guggenheim, nr.439\"."@ca .

